    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d667">

                <pb facs="0786" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg666"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-08-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 22, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8. Montenegrin series.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the
                    Official Gazette of Montenegro published a few days ago a decree of the Prince
                    authorizing a parliament, which will probably meet next December for the first
                    time, and also granting freedom of the press. Until now the legislative power in
                    Montenegro has been in the hands of a council of state, consisting of the crown
                    prince, the metropolitan, and the members of the cabinet. …</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles S.
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
